Description: Keep the emulated mode's size for a fullscreen X client
 Xwayland lets a client set a lower display mode and emulates it: it lists
 the mode's rectangle in _XWAYLAND_RANDR_EMU_MONITOR_RECTS on the client's
 windows and scales a window of that size at the output's origin to the
 output through wp_viewport. The window manager resized such a window to the
 output when the shell made it fullscreen, as kiosk-shell does each
 toplevel, so the client's frame drew unscaled in the corner of a window
 larger than its mode. The window manager now reads the property, gives a
 fullscreen window the emulated size in its configure, fullscreens it again
 when the property changes, keeps the window at the output's origin while
 the shell centres the smaller surface, and takes input over the whole
 scaled surface.
Author: Rach2
Forwarded: no
